Amputation  
 
Amputation is defined as the full or partial severing of a limb, and is extremely 
traumatic for the casualty.  The priority here is to stop the bleeding, then 
preserve  the amputated limb and reassure the casualty.  
 Immediately treat the casualty for bleeding ( see page 36) and shock ( see page 
33). 
 Dial 999 for an ambulance immediately.  
 Cover the wound with a low adherent, non-fluffy  dressing.  
 If possible, wrap the  amputated part in a plastic bag and place on or in  a bag of 
ice to preserve it as much as possible.  Do not allow the amputated part to 
be in contact with the ice or get wet in any way.  
  
Crush injuries  
 
This type of injury usually occurs on building site s or at road traffic accidents.  
If the flow of blood to a limb ( such as an arm or leg ) is restricted by a crushing 
weight, there is the serious danger of a build -up of toxins in the muscle tissue
