[2026-10-06T07:55:53.612Z] INFO faser.utils_med: If you fail to support the neck and spine of an unconscious person while moving them, it can lead to serious complications. Specifically:

- The airway may become obstructed due to vomit or a tongue falling back.
- This obstruction can prevent breathing, leading to suffocation.
- Failure to maintain an open airway can result in death.

The correct approach involves supporting both the head and neck while performing CPR (cardiopulmonary resuscitation) until professional medical help arrives. It's crucial to ensure the spine remains stable during transport to avoid further injury.
