[2026-10-06T07:56:13.544Z] INFO faser.utils_med: To minimize pain during the movement of someone with a fractured leg to safety:
1. Immobilize the lower leg using splints extended from the groin to just below the foot.
2. Ensure the splints remain securely in place throughout the process.
3. Have the first aider tie all knots on the splint for comfort.
4. Position broad bandages around the thigh, knee, ankle, and above and below the fracture site.
5. Begin tying the bandages starting at the thigh and working down towards the foot.
6. At the ankles, use a figure-of-eight knot instead of regular knots.
7. Keep the injured person's legs together and stabilized as much as possible.
8. Avoid letting go of the leg until instructed by the first aider, who will tell when it's safe to release the bandages.
9. Be gentle but firm during the movement, ensuring proper alignment and stability.
10. Stay calm and provide reassurance to both the injured person and others assisting.
By following these steps, you can help reduce discomfort and facilitate the safer transfer of the injured individual to safety.
